{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1087", "sample_idx": 47, "model_name": "mistralai/mixtral-8x7b-instruct-v0.1", "content": " the social network is a 2010 film directed by david fincher and written by aaron sorkin. it tells the story of the founding of facebook by mark zuckerberg and the legal battles that followed.\n\nnote that there are some liberties taken with the true story for the sake of dramatization.\n\nthe film opens in 2003, with zuckerberg, played by jesse eisenberg, being dumped by his girlfriend. in a fit of pique, he creates a website called \"facemash,\" which allows users to compare the pictures of two female students and vote on which one is more attractive. the site quickly becomes popular, crashing harvard's servers and getting zuckerberg in trouble with the university administration.\n\n\nhowever, the idea of a social networking site is born, and zuckerberg teams up with his friend eduardo saverin, played by andrew garfield, to create \"thefacebook.\" the site quickly gains users, and zuckerberg brings on two other partners, the winklevoss twins, played by armie hammer, who had originally approached him with the idea for a social networking site for harvard students.\n\n\nhowever, as thefacebook grows in popularity, tensions rise between the partners, and zuckerberg is sued by both saverin and the winklevoss twins. the film then jumps to 2008, where zuckerberg is called to testify in a deposition for the lawsuits.\n\n\nthroughout the film, we see zuckerberg as a brilliant but socially awkward individual who is driven to create something that will make him respected and powerful. eisenberg's portrayal of zuckerberg is nuanced and compelling, and he effectively conveys the character's ambition, insecurity, and arrogance.\n\n\nthe supporting cast is also strong, with garfield, hammer, and justin timberlake, who plays napster founder sean parker, all delivering solid performances. the film's script, by sorkin, is fast-paced and witty, and the direction by fincher is stylish and propulsive.\n\n\nthe social network is a fascinating exploration of the creation of one of the most influential companies of the 21st century, and it is a must-see for anyone interested in technology, entrepreneurship, or the human drama behind the headlines. it is a well-crafted film that is both entertaining and thought-provoking.", "logprobs": [{"token": "the", "logprob": -0.0023255704436451197}, {"token": "social", "logprob": -2.861018856492592e-06}, {"token": "network", "logprob": -3.8742269680369645e-05}, {"token": "is", "logprob": -4.494089080253616e-05}, {"token": "a", "logprob": -2.50339189733495e-06}, {"token": "", "logprob": -2.2116448879241943}, {"token": "2", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "0", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "1", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "0", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "film", "logprob": -0.17916493117809296}, {"token": "directed", "logprob": -0.002476127352565527}, {"token": "by", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "d", "logprob": -0.00013362467871047556}, {"token": "avid", "logprob": -2.3841855067985307e-07}, {"token": "fin", "logprob": -0.0033660440240055323}, {"token": "cher", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "and", "logprob": -0.008083485998213291}, {"token": "written", "logprob": -7.319182623177767e-05}, {"token": "by", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "a", "logprob": -0.0001392267586197704}, {"token": "aron", "logprob": -1.1920928244535389e-07}, {"token": "s", "logprob": -0.00023469554434996098}, {"token": "ork", "logprob": -0.00011920218821614981}, {"token": "in", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": ".", "logprob": -1.4045289754867554}, {"token": "it", "logprob": -0.14793387055397034}, {"token": "tells", "logprob": -0.44167089462280273}, {"token": "the", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "story", "logprob": -0.0006400682032108307}, {"token": "of", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "the", "logprob": -0.001704074558801949}, {"token": "founding", "logprob": -0.06227995082736015}, {"token": "of", "logprob": -2.861018856492592e-06}, {"token": "face",